te $67$ as an integer multiple of $6,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $67≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ because\n\n$$\n67=11\\cdot 6+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $67$ modulo $6$ is $1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}67 & ≡67-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡67-11\\cdot 6 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡67-66 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $67$ modulo $6$ is $1.$" 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412371 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412367 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412371 1069 "q-213089" 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412371 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412371 1071 "$-54\\text{ mod }7=${{field-1}}" 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412371 1072 #uuid "0a2135af-f11d-5278-a560-c7cd73d93e86" 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412371 1074 "The residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is the integer $0\\le r<7$ such that\n\n$$\n-54≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-54$ as an integer multiple of $7,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-54≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ because\n\n$$\n-54=(-8)\\cdot 7+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is $2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-54 & ≡-54+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-54+8\\cdot 7 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-54+56 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡2 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is $2.$" 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412372 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412361 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412372 1069 "q-76973" 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412372 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [17592186412372 1071 "$-21\\text{ mod }5=$" 13194139534149 17592186045417 true] [175921864